## Implementation Approach

The original script uses packet manipulation:
- Hook `SMSG_LIST_INVENTORY` (0x19F) to send custom vendor data
- Hook `CMSG_BUY_ITEM` (0x1A2) and `CMSG_BUY_ITEM_IN_SLOT` (0x1A3) for purchases

```lua
-- Packet events
local PACKET_EVENT_ON_PACKET_RECEIVE = 5
local PACKET_EVENT_ON_PACKET_SEND    = 7
local SMSG_LIST_INVENTORY            = 0x19F
local CMSG_BUY_ITEM                  = 0x1A2
local CMSG_BUY_ITEM_IN_SLOT          = 0x1A3

RegisterPacketEvent(SMSG_LIST_INVENTORY, PACKET_EVENT_ON_PACKET_SEND, SendUpdatedVendorList)
RegisterPacketEvent(CMSG_BUY_ITEM, PACKET_EVENT_ON_PACKET_RECEIVE, ReceiveItemBought)
```

### Vendor Packet Structure
```lua
-- Per item in vendor list:
packet:WriteGUID(vendorGUID)
packet:WriteULong(slot)           -- 1-indexed
packet:WriteULong(item.id)
packet:WriteULong(displayInfoID)
packet:WriteLong(leftInStock)     -- -1 for unlimited
packet:WriteULong(price)
packet:WriteULong(maxDurability)
packet:WriteULong(buyCount)
packet:WriteULong(extendedCost)
```

